What this solution actually does: a timer-driven Windows worker processes confirmed user-administration requests and synchronizes clients, accounts, email addresses, tokens and permissions across CMS, TOMI and TOMSER. It also unblocks IPs, processes queued scripts and runs startup-labelled inactivity/password checks. General processes run in explicit order before startup-labelled processes on the first eligible application invocation. Operations depend on shared MUFG_T24 configuration/service-control facilities. No HTTP API or message listener is evidenced in this solution.
